1
00:00:02,100 --> 00:00:06,360
Your price alerts are listed on the Summary tab, under Price Alerts.

2
00:00:06,460 --> 00:00:09,070
Right-click the list to manage your alerts.

3
00:00:09,170 --> 00:00:15,380
Choose Add Alert to create a new one.

4
00:00:15,480 --> 00:00:19,290
Type the instrument and pick it from the list.

5
00:00:19,390 --> 00:00:22,650
Choose whether to watch the Bid or the Ask price.

6
00:00:22,750 --> 00:00:26,310
The rate starts at the current price. Type the price you want.

7
00:00:26,410 --> 00:00:33,590
The line below tells you what will trigger the alert.

8
00:00:33,690 --> 00:00:37,950
Alerts are saved on the server, so they stay when you log in again.

9
00:00:38,050 --> 00:00:43,090
Double-click an alert, or right-click and choose Edit Alert, to change it.

10
00:00:43,190 --> 00:00:50,880
Change the rate, then click Save.

11
00:00:50,980 --> 00:00:54,100
Remove Alert deletes one alert.

12
00:00:54,200 --> 00:01:03,380
You are asked to confirm first. Click Remove.

13
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:09,110
This alert is left at the current price, so it fires almost at once.

14
00:01:09,210 --> 00:01:18,890
When the price is reached, a notification appears and the alert is removed.

15
00:01:18,990 --> 00:01:29,740
Remove All Alerts clears the whole list.

